<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    SPIKE-02 throwaway render page (deleted in Task 3 per D-05).

    This page is an INSTRUMENT, not a screen. It is the thinnest layout that puts
    SettingsCard, DataGrid and WrapPanel on screen simultaneously and nothing else.
    No theming, no styling, no padding tuning beyond what keeps the controls from
    being clipped — anything more would be decoration on an instrument whose only
    output is "does this render, and is it themed like WinUI".

    NAMESPACE RESOLUTION IS PART OF THE FINDING (D-07: record, do not diagnose).
    Every prefix below was read out of the ASSEMBLY METADATA of the pinned package
    (its own XML doc file, which lists T: members), never guessed. NONE of the three
    matched the plan's expectation, and reaching the correct set took three build
    attempts. The FINAL, BUILDING mapping is:

      - SettingsCard  -> CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls
      - WrapPanel     -> CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls
      - DataGrid      -> CommunityToolkit.WinUI.UI.Controls

    The plan (and 01-RESEARCH.md) predicted per-package namespaces for the 8.2 train
    (Controls.SettingsControls, Controls.Primitives). The 8.2 assemblies declare BOTH
    types directly in the flattened namespace CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls; the
    per-package names appear in the assemblies only as ASSEMBLY names, which is the
    trap. DataGrid, frozen at 7.1.2, sits in a different namespace again -
    CommunityToolkit.WinUI.UI.Controls - and NOT in the legacy
    Microsoft.Toolkit.Uwp.UI.Controls.DataGrid the plan predicted.

    Each superseded prefix produced a verbatim compiler error, all recorded in the
    verdict's Configuration findings section. They are NAMESPACE-RESOLUTION findings
    about where a type is declared - they say nothing about whether a control renders,
    and they are NOT rendering verdicts.
-->
<Window
    x:Class="AkariTool.Spike.WinUiControlCompat.MainWindow"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:toolkitControls="using:CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls"
    xmlns:dataGridControls="using:CommunityToolkit.WinUI.UI.Controls"
    Title="SPIKE-02 — WinUI control compatibility probe">

    <Grid Margin="16" RowSpacing="16">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- 1. SettingsCard — CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls.SettingsControls 8.2.251219,
                type CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls.SettingsCard -->
        <StackPanel Grid.Row="0" Spacing="8">
            <TextBlock Text="SettingsCard (SettingsControls 8.2.251219)"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" />
            <toolkitControls:SettingsCard Header="SPIKE-02 SettingsCard"
                                          Description="CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls.SettingsControls"
                                          Width="420">
                <TextBlock Text="SettingsCard body content" />
            </toolkitControls:SettingsCard>
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- 2. WrapPanel — CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls.Primitives 8.2.251219,
                type CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls.WrapPanel. Eight children so that
                wrapping is visually unambiguous: if these eight boxes all sit on ONE
                line, the control did not lay out. -->
        <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Spacing="8">
            <TextBlock Text="WrapPanel (Primitives 8.2.251219)"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" />
            <toolkitControls:WrapPanel HorizontalSpacing="8" VerticalSpacing="8" Width="420">
                <Border Width="88" Height="40" Background="#3F7FD1">
                    <TextBlock Text="1" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Border>
                <Border Width="88" Height="40" Background="#5BA85F">
                    <TextBlock Text="2" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Border>
                <Border Width="88" Height="40" Background="#C97A3D">
                    <TextBlock Text="3" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Border>
                <Border Width="88" Height="40" Background="#9B59B6">
                    <TextBlock Text="4" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Border>
                <Border Width="88" Height="40" Background="#34495E">
                    <TextBlock Text="5" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Border>
                <Border Width="88" Height="40" Background="#16A085">
                    <TextBlock Text="6" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Border>
                <Border Width="88" Height="40" Background="#D35454">
                    <TextBlock Text="7" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Border>
                <Border Width="88" Height="40" Background="#7F8C8D">
                    <TextBlock Text="8" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Border>
            </toolkitControls:WrapPanel>
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- 3. DataGrid — CommunityToolkit.WinUI.UI.Controls.DataGrid 7.1.2 (type and
                namespace share the CommunityToolkit.WinUI.UI.Controls prefix; see the
                header note). AutoGenerateColumns plus two DataGridTextColumns over a
                real ItemsSource, so ROWS are painted rather than just headers: a grid
                that renders only its column headers is a distinct symptom from one that
                renders nothing at all. -->
        <StackPanel Grid.Row="2" Spacing="8">
            <TextBlock Text="DataGrid (DataGrid 7.1.2 — frozen, last published 2021-11-18)"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" />
            <dataGridControls:DataGrid x:Name="ProbeDataGrid"
                                       AutoGenerateColumns="True"
                                       Width="560"
                                       Height="200"
                                       ItemsSource="{x:Bind ProbeRows, Mode=OneTime}">
                <dataGridControls:DataGrid.Columns>
                    <dataGridControls:DataGridTextColumn Header="Name" Binding="{Binding Name}" />
                    <dataGridControls:DataGridTextColumn Header="Value" Binding="{Binding Value}" />
                </dataGridControls:DataGrid.Columns>
            </dataGridControls:DataGrid>
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</Window>
